- node_id: family_sequential
- base_node_id: root
- title: Sequential coupling evaluation
- difficulty_1_to_5: 4
- description: Implement one Triton program that evaluates the three convolutions of a single coupling transform over a bounded batch-time tile, retaining small temporal/channel intermediates where practical and materializing only the transform result.
- expected_vs_baseline_factor: 1.20x
- rationale: The reference performs 12 separate convolutions per invocation and materializes every intermediate. Reducing kernel boundaries and intermediate global traffic should help moderate and large workloads while preserving the reference layer order.

